    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n64539" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαι-ευτικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>skilled in midwifery</i>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				151c
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ μαιευτικὴ τέχνη</span> or
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ -κή</span> alone, art <i>of
				delivery</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Plt.</u>
				268b
			</span></i>; esp. metaph. of the Socratic method of eliciting from
			others what was in their minds without their knowing it, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Tht.</u>
				161e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				3.49s
			</span></i>q.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ μ. διάλογοι</span> of
			Plato, such as <i><span class="en">
				<u>Alc.</u>
				1
			</span></i>, <i>La., Ly.</i>, Thrasyll.ib.<i><span class="en">
				59
			</span></i>. Adv. -
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Poll.
					4.208
				</span></i>
			.</div>
